{"cross_mech":[],"family":{"alphafold_models":12534,"candidate_reasons":["pfam_previous_unknown_name"],"characterization_status":"","context_evidence_count":null,"cross_mech":{"example_proteins":0,"protein_traits_record":false,"records_by_mech":{},"scanned":false},"curation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","demotion_reasons":[],"description":"The bacterial Tat system has a remarkable ability to transport folded proteins even enzyme complexes across the cytoplasmic membrane. It is structurally and mechanistically similar to the Delta pH-driven thylakoidal protein import pathway. A functional Tat system or Delta pH-dependent pathway requires three integral membrane proteins: TatA/Tha4, TatB/Hcf106 and TatC/cpTatC. The TatC protein is essential for the function of both pathways. It might be involved in twin-arginine signal peptide recognition, protein translocation and proton translocation. Sequence analysis predicts that TatC contains six transmembrane helices (TMHs), and experimental data confirmed that N- and C-termini of TatC or cpTatC are exposed to the cytoplasmic or stromal face of the membrane. The cytoplasmic N-terminus and the first cytoplasmic loop region of the Escherichia coli TatC protein are essential for protein export. At least two TatC molecules co-exist within each Tat translocon [[cite:PUB00011123]].","domain_architectures":28,"interpro_id":"IPR002033","known_evidence_count":null,"matches":19252,"name":"Sec-independent protein translocase protein (TatC)","partial_evidence_count":null,"pfam_id":"PF00902","proteins":18890,"proteomes":16293,"short_name":"TatC","source_url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/api/entry/pfam/PF00902","structures":11,"taxa":23768,"unknown_status":"EX_DUF"},"inputs":{"cross_mech":"cross-mech-duf-examples-2026-10-10","members":"pfam-uniprot-uniref90-2026-10-07","protein_examples":"duf-protein-examples-direct-2026-10-13","worklist":"interpro-pfam-duf-2026-10-10"},"members":[],"metadata":{"curation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","history":[{"action":"CREATE","agent":"Codex","curator":"Codex","description":"Inspected Frobel 2012 primary Methods, Results, Discussion and Figures 1-4, the cited Orriss pFAT588 construct method, and UniProt/InterPro member mapping. Three graphs retain five directly observed assay effects while separating signal cleavage from protected mature-product transport and excluding purified TatC sufficiency or observed hairpin microsteps. Minimal evidence caches and explicit unresolved contexts accompany an IN_PROGRESS overlay; schema validation passed. Whole-family review and publication remain incomplete.","event_index":0,"history_record":"history/records/PF00902/2026-10-11T080327Z-codex-10524c.yaml","llm_assisted":true,"local_source":"source/history/records/PF00902/2026-10-11T080327Z-codex-10524c.yaml","outcome":"changed","source_path":"history/records/PF00902/2026-10-11T080327Z-codex-10524c.yaml","summary":"Curate scoped TatC vesicle transport and precursor-processing graphs","timestamp":"2026-10-11T08:03:27Z","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/DUFMech/blob/af999e086a21eae74387fc5bcd1a31b3ae2f4ed2/history/records/PF00902/2026-10-11T080327Z-codex-10524c.yaml"},{"action":"REVIEW","agent":"Codex","curator":"Codex","description":"Saved current-content review 20261011T081604Z-pf00902-tatc-vesicle-processing-and-transport with digest af32143d43ccccc72094d5ac504f75e05d14df5b16216f4e1fe842bd5dea04c2. Native schema, graph evidence and overlay-projection checks pass; full records regeneration changed only two family projections and ownership manifest. Five observed edges remain limited to three native vesicle contexts, with incomplete constructs, methods, other substrates and insertion microsteps retained as open coverage. Same-agent review, not independent endorsement; status remains IN_PROGRESS.","event_index":0,"history_record":"history/records/PF00902/2026-10-11T081608Z-codex-ca36fb.yaml","llm_assisted":true,"local_source":"source/history/records/PF00902/2026-10-11T081608Z-codex-ca36fb.yaml","outcome":"needs_followup","source_path":"history/records/PF00902/2026-10-11T081608Z-codex-ca36fb.yaml","summary":"Retain partial scientific self-review of TatC vesicle causal effects","timestamp":"2026-10-11T08:16:08Z","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/DUFMech/blob/af999e086a21eae74387fc5bcd1a31b3ae2f4ed2/history/records/PF00902/2026-10-11T081608Z-codex-ca36fb.yaml"}],"local_source":"source/data/families/PF00902.yaml","record":{"causal_graphs":[{"context":"BL21(DE3) DeltaTat produces vesicles with p8737 tatABCD. Radiolabeled TorA-MalE335 lacks 35 C-terminal MalE residues; vesicles are added 10 min after translation starts, followed by 25 min at 37 C. No-vesicle, TatAC and proteinase-K comparisons distinguish processing from protection. CCCP is 0.1 mM, compared with DMSO vehicle.","edges":[{"directness":"DIRECT","edge_id":"tat-system-produces-protected-product","evidence":[{"cache_path":"evidence/PF00902/froebel-2012-tatC.txt","cache_sha256":"c4afb4ff69ccb0166e8c4cc072032b43a751ff6c4ac265808a1c8d1367cc6112","explanation":"Figure 1A lanes 1-6 and Figure 3A distinguish the Tat-positive protected mature band from TatAC premature cleavage. Adopted molecular readout is the gel/protease endpoint, not the Figure 4B insertion cartoon.","reference":"PMID:23250441","snippet":"premature cleavage","source_url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3538955/"},{"cache_path":"evidence/PF00902/TatC-identity.txt","cache_sha256":"d50c23c5360ed27148ed782082193a8ca9d7f0f55b6f912649521c119aa225d7","explanation":"Verifies the TatC family mapping without converting a profile interval into the experimental construct.","reference":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/api/protein/uniprot/P69423/entry/pfam/PF00902/","snippet":"P69423 Pfam:PF00902 interval: 12-221, inclusive","source_url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/api/protein/uniprot/P69423/entry/pfam/PF00902/"}],"evidence_kind":"EXPERIMENTAL","mechanism":"The joint vesicle and precursor preparation yields a processed mature band that survives external proteinase K. The no-vesicle precursor is digested; the TatAC processed band lacks protection. The cause is the complete assay system, not independently sufficient TatC.","object":"protected-mature-male335","predicate":"produces","subject":"tat-positive-precursor-system","support":"OBSERVED"},{"directness":"DIRECT","edge_id":"cccp-decreases-protected-product","evidence":[{"cache_path":"evidence/PF00902/froebel-2012-tatC.txt","cache_sha256":"c4afb4ff69ccb0166e8c4cc072032b43a751ff6c4ac265808a1c8d1367cc6112","explanation":"Figure 3A lanes 5-8 show loss of the Tat-positive processed/protected response with CCCP. The TatAC cleavage in lanes 9-12 persists and is not merged into this transport endpoint.","reference":"PMID:23250441","snippet":"premature cleavage","source_url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3538955/"}],"evidence_kind":"EXPERIMENTAL","mechanism":"CCCP removes the detected Tat-positive protected mature-product response relative to the vehicle condition. This is an assay-level energetic perturbation, not identification of TatC as its unique molecular target.","object":"protected-mature-male335","predicate":"decreases","subject":"cccp-transport-perturbation","support":"OBSERVED"}],"family_mapping":"K-12 TatC reference UniProtKB:P69423, tatC/b3839/JW3815, has 258 residues, sequence version 2, and PF00902 at 12-221 inclusive with exact UniProt/InterPro sequence agreement. The assay uses full-length Tat proteins and native membrane components; reference taxon is not the BL21 production strain. Complete p8737 clone junctions were not reconstructed.","graph_id":"tatc-containing-vesicle-protein-transport","limitations":"Protection supports transport into vesicles, not a directly filmed microscopic pathway. CCCP perturbs membrane energetics, not TatC alone; no TatC proton-pump activity is asserted. Buffer and protease details rely on cited protocols, and raw gels, quantitative transport rates and supplement data were not reanalyzed.","nodes":[{"grounding":["UniProtKB:P69423"],"label":"Tat-positive inverted vesicles plus TorA-MalE335 precursor","node_id":"tat-positive-precursor-system","node_type":"ACTIVITY"},{"label":"Addition of 0.1 mM CCCP to the Tat-positive assay","node_id":"cccp-transport-perturbation","node_type":"PERTURBATION"},{"label":"Proteinase-K-protected mature MalE335 product","node_id":"protected-mature-male335","node_type":"STATE"}],"scope":"Intact E. coli Tat machinery in inverted membrane vesicles, not purified TatC or an isolated PF00902 fragment. Adopted readout is mature-product protection from proteinase K.","scope_status":"MECHANISTIC","taxon":"NCBITaxon:562","title":"Tat-positive vesicles generate protease-protected mature TorA-MalE335"},{"context":"BL21(DE3) DeltaTat with p8737-tatAC; translation/vesicle reaction at 37 C for 25 min after vesicle addition. RR TorA-MalE335 from pPJ1 is compared with its RR-to-KK counterpart from pPJ2. Proteinase-K exposure tests accessibility, and Tat-positive vesicles provide a transport comparator.","edges":[{"directness":"DIRECT","edge_id":"tatac-system-produces-accessible-product","evidence":[{"cache_path":"evidence/PF00902/froebel-2012-tatC.txt","cache_sha256":"c4afb4ff69ccb0166e8c4cc072032b43a751ff6c4ac265808a1c8d1367cc6112","explanation":"Figures 1A and 2A show processing in the TatAC lanes followed by disappearance of mature product on proteinase-K treatment, unlike Tat-positive protection.","reference":"PMID:23250441","snippet":"premature cleavage","source_url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3538955/"}],"evidence_kind":"EXPERIMENTAL","mechanism":"TatAC vesicles generate a mature-size MalE335 band without protection of that product against added protease. Vesicle-associated processing and exposure of the passenger are jointly retained; successful full-protein export is not inferred.","object":"accessible-processed-male335","predicate":"produces","subject":"tatac-rr-precursor-system","support":"OBSERVED"},{"directness":"DIRECT","edge_id":"rr-to-kk-decreases-tatac-processing","evidence":[{"cache_path":"evidence/PF00902/froebel-2012-tatC.txt","cache_sha256":"c4afb4ff69ccb0166e8c4cc072032b43a751ff6c4ac265808a1c8d1367cc6112","explanation":"Figure 2A compares RR TatAC lanes 5-6 with KK lanes 11-12. The cleavage-site mutant in panel C belongs to TorA-PhoA, not MalE335, and is not borrowed for this edge.","reference":"PMID:23250441","snippet":"premature cleavage","source_url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3538955/"}],"evidence_kind":"EXPERIMENTAL","mechanism":"Replacing the precursor twin arginines with lysines eliminates detected TatAC processing under the comparison conditions. The change is scoped to this precursor and assay rather than a universal recognition rule for every family member.","object":"accessible-processed-male335","predicate":"decreases","subject":"tatac-kk-precursor-replacement","support":"OBSERVED"}],"family_mapping":"TatC P69423 maps to PF00902 residues 12-221, within a 258-residue reference. This intact-protein/native-membrane preparation also includes TatA and signal peptidase. No isolated Pfam interval or all-Tat-substrate transfer is supported.","graph_id":"tatac-premature-precursor-processing","limitations":"Cleavage alone does not show transport of the mature passenger. RR-to-KK is a signal-peptide change, not a TatC mutation or direct binding measurement. Natural SufI/AmiC and linker variants have different cleavage behavior; the proposed hairpin topology remains a model. Complete clone sequences and referenced assay details remain open.","nodes":[{"grounding":["UniProtKB:P69423"],"label":"TatAC vesicles plus RR TorA-MalE335 precursor","node_id":"tatac-rr-precursor-system","node_type":"ACTIVITY"},{"label":"RR-to-KK precursor replacement in the TatAC assay","node_id":"tatac-kk-precursor-replacement","node_type":"PERTURBATION"},{"label":"Processed MalE335 product accessible to proteinase K","node_id":"accessible-processed-male335","node_type":"STATE"}],"scope":"TatB-lacking inverted vesicles expressing TatA and TatC; observed precursor cleavage is separate from mature-protein transport.","scope_status":"MECHANISTIC","taxon":"NCBITaxon:562","title":"TatAC vesicles process TorA-MalE335 without protecting its mature domain"},{"context":"BL21(DE3) DeltaTat with pFAT588 produces TatC-containing vesicles. The cited plasmid is pQE60-derived with MC4100 tatC and a C-terminal His6 tag. Figure 4A compares TatC, TatAC, Tat-positive and DeltaTat vesicles in the 37 C translation/processing reaction; Figure 1B verifies Tat-component content.","edges":[{"directness":"DIRECT","edge_id":"tatc-vesicles-produce-accessible-product","evidence":[{"cache_path":"evidence/PF00902/froebel-2012-tatC.txt","cache_sha256":"c4afb4ff69ccb0166e8c4cc072032b43a751ff6c4ac265808a1c8d1367cc6112","explanation":"Figure 4A lower panel lanes 7-10 establishes the TatC-versus-DeltaTat processing comparison and lack of mature-product protection. Figure 4B supplies a proposed explanation, not another observed edge.","reference":"PMID:23250441","snippet":"premature cleavage","source_url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3538955/"},{"cache_path":"evidence/PF00902/orriss-2007-tatC-construct.txt","cache_sha256":"d500aca67df3bfc675eced3b7b2c5e989fb798e0990073669eedf3e5200b9192","explanation":"The cited construct method resolves pFAT588's tag orientation and MC4100 DNA origin, not a purified-protein version of the later vesicle assay.","reference":"PMID:17686475","snippet":"TatC with a hexa-histidine tag on the C-terminus","source_url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2517984/"}],"evidence_kind":"EXPERIMENTAL","mechanism":"TatC-containing vesicles produce a mature-size band that is digested by proteinase K. DeltaTat vesicles generate degradation fragments but not the corresponding mature band; all native vesicle components remain part of the tested system.","object":"tatc-accessible-mature-product","predicate":"produces","subject":"tatc-only-precursor-system","support":"OBSERVED"}],"family_mapping":"Native TatC reference P69423, 258 residues, sequence version 2, PF00902 at 12-221. The source identifies the pFAT588 lineage and C-terminal tag but complete 2012 clone junctions were not independently sequenced. Native reference, MC4100 DNA donor and BL21 vesicle host are distinct identifiers.","graph_id":"tatc-only-vesicle-processing","limitations":"Native membrane, resident signal peptidase and precursor remain required assay context. The result does not demonstrate purified TatC sufficiency, an atomic insertion trajectory or transport of the mature passenger. It cannot be generalized to every signal peptide, and the separate pPJ10 in-vivo construct is not this vesicle construct.","nodes":[{"grounding":["UniProtKB:P69423"],"label":"TatC-only Tat-component vesicles plus TorA-MalE335","node_id":"tatc-only-precursor-system","node_type":"ACTIVITY"},{"label":"Mature-size MalE335 product without protease protection","node_id":"tatc-accessible-mature-product","node_type":"STATE"}],"scope":"TatC-only refers to the supplied Tat components in native inverted vesicles, not purified TatC alone. Adopted endpoint is TorA-MalE335 processing without mature-product protease protection.","scope_status":"MECHANISTIC","taxon":"NCBITaxon:562","title":"TatC as the sole Tat component supports premature precursor processing"}],"characterization_status":"UNSCORED","counters":{"alphafold_models":12534,"domain_architectures":28,"matches":19252,"proteins":18890,"proteomes":16293,"structures":11,"taxa":23768},"curation_events":[{"action":"CREATE","curator":"Codex","event_index":0,"history_record":"history/records/PF00902/2026-10-11T080327Z-codex-10524c.yaml","llm_assisted":true,"outcome":"changed","summary":"Curate scoped TatC vesicle transport and precursor-processing graphs","timestamp":"2026-10-11T08:03:27Z"},{"action":"REVIEW","curator":"Codex","event_index":0,"history_record":"history/records/PF00902/2026-10-11T081608Z-codex-ca36fb.yaml","llm_assisted":true,"outcome":"needs_followup","summary":"Retain partial scientific self-review of TatC vesicle causal effects","timestamp":"2026-10-11T08:16:08Z"}],"curation_history":"history/records/PF00902","curation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","description":"The bacterial Tat system has a remarkable ability to transport folded proteins even enzyme complexes across the cytoplasmic membrane. It is structurally and mechanistically similar to the Delta pH-driven thylakoidal protein import pathway. A functional Tat system or Delta pH-dependent pathway requires three integral membrane proteins: TatA/Tha4, TatB/Hcf106 and TatC/cpTatC. The TatC protein is essential for the function of both pathways. It might be involved in twin-arginine signal peptide recognition, protein translocation and proton translocation. Sequence analysis predicts that TatC contains six transmembrane helices (TMHs), and experimental data confirmed that N- and C-termini of TatC or cpTatC are exposed to the cytoplasmic or stromal face of the membrane. The cytoplasmic N-terminus and the first cytoplasmic loop region of the Escherichia coli TatC protein are essential for protein export. At least two TatC molecules co-exist within each Tat translocon [[cite:PUB00011123]].","discussions":[{"discussion_id":"tatc-insertion-model-and-family-coverage","evidence":[{"evidence_source":"full_text","explanation":"Adopted Figures 1-4 separate processing, protease protection, RR specificity and energetic sensitivity. Figure 5 and Discussion expose substrate/linker dependence and model assumptions; in-vivo, structural and additional substrate contexts remain uncurated.","reference":"PMID:23250441","supports":"PARTIAL"},{"evidence_source":"selected_full_text","explanation":"The cited pFAT588 method establishes MC4100 origin and a C-terminal His6 tag. Complete later plasmid sequence and the other constructs remain incompletely verified.","reference":"PMID:17686475","supports":"PARTIAL"}],"kind":"CURATION_TODO","notes":"Inspect supplements, referenced reaction/protease methods and later primary structure or translocation experiments. Preserve all native vesicle components in sufficiency claims. Other taxa, TatC paralogs and signal substrates need separate mapping and tests. This partial self-reviewed entry remains IN_PROGRESS.","posed_by":"Codex","posed_date":"2026-10-11","prompt":"Resolve TatC insertion microsteps and extend beyond the TorA-MalE335 vesicle assays.","rationale":"Signal-peptide processing and mature-domain transport are distinct observations. Proposed hairpin insertion, TatB shielding and TatA assembly require their own evidence before becoming observed molecular edges.","status":"OPEN"}],"id":"Pfam:PF00902","interpro_id":"InterPro:IPR002033","name":"Sec-independent protein translocase protein (TatC)","pfam_id":"PF00902","provenance":{"generated_at":"2026-10-10T07:44:21.614711Z","path":"data/worklists/interpro-pfam-duf-2026-10-10.json","sha256":"17fb625876c9326ed284263a47bcd84e0d7844a31c040dc06cd2260c36f1c383","snapshot_id":"interpro-pfam-duf-2026-10-10","source_url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/api/entry/pfam/"},"seed_status":"EX_DUF","short_name":"TatC","source_url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/api/entry/pfam/PF00902"},"reviews":[{"label":"2026-10-11T08:16:04Z: NEEDS_FOLLOWUP by Codex","local_source":"source/reviews/structured/20261011T081604Z-pf00902-tatc-vesicle-processing-and-transport/review.yaml","scientific_review":true,"scope":"Scientific assessment of the retained edges, exact member mapping, primary evidence, context and causal limits.","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/DUFMech/blob/af999e086a21eae74387fc5bcd1a31b3ae2f4ed2/reviews/structured/20261011T081604Z-pf00902-tatc-vesicle-processing-and-transport/review.yaml"}],"source":{"commit":"af999e086a21eae74387fc5bcd1a31b3ae2f4ed2","path":"data/families/PF00902.yaml","repository":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/DUFMech","sha256":"09c55d30f0ea3e9cb5c38846e2caa8474d84866d0df555bf0e7ff17e7ba2819d